{title: The First Noel}
{key: G}
{time: 3/4}

The [G]first No[D]el the [C]angel did [G]say,
Was to [C]certain poor [Bm]shepherds in [C]fields as [D]they [G]lay;
In [G]fields where [D]they lay [C]keeping their [G]sheep,
On a [C]cold winter's [Bm]night that [C]was [D]so [G]deep.

{label: Chorus}
[G]Noel, [D]Noel, [C]Noel, [G]Noel,
[C]Born is the [Bm]King of [C]Is[D]ra[G]el.

They [G]looked up [D]and saw [C]a [G]star,
[C]Shining in [Bm]the east, be[C]yond [D]them [G]far;
And [G]to the [D]earth it [C]gave great [G]light,
And [C]so it [Bm]continued [C]both day [D]and [G]night.

{label: Chorus}
[G]Noel, [D]Noel, [C]Noel, [G]Noel,
[C]Born is the [Bm]King of [C]Is[D]ra[G]el.

Then [G]entered [D]in those [C]wise men [G]three,
Full [C]reverently [Bm]upon [C]their [D]kn[G]ee,
And [G]offered [D]there in [C]His pres[G]ence,
[C]Their gold [Bm]and myrrh [C]and [D]frank[G]incense.

{label: Chorus}
[G]Noel, [D]Noel, [C]Noel, [G]Noel,
[C]Born is the [Bm]King of [C]Is[D]ra[G]el.
